From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:46:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 520/520] [DS4.1] Programmatic dependent launch along the
 decode chain

A decode step is one chain of about 1,850 kernels in CUDA graphs. On its
critical path (request-inventory-5's rank-0 traces) the graph-internal launch
gaps between consecutive kernels of one capture stream are 3.5% of a
one-stream greedy step (median 0.51 us), 4.5% sampled and 1.6% at eight
streams; cross-stream joins are under 0.01%.

Every kernel on the layer chain now begins with pdl.chain():
griddepcontrol.wait before any global access, so a kernel sees exactly what
a serialized launch would, then launch_dependents, so the next kernel's
launch and CTA start-up overlap this one's body. TileLang marks a kernel that
waits for programmatic stream serialization, which CUDA graph capture keeps
as a programmatic edge. Kernels: mHC entry, finalize, post and collapse; the
decode MXFP8 GEMMs, split-K partials and reduces, WO-A; RoPE, cache writes,
sparse-MLA metadata and attention, the indexer and compressor; MoE dispatch,
grouped GEMMs, SwiGLU cast and combine; routing; the shared expert's SwiGLU.
TileKernels' casts and norms use DeepSeek's own switch (pdl.tile_kernels).

The warp-specialized GEMMs keep their launch (gemm_bf16, gemm_bf16_two and
gemm_bf16_partials: the router and the other BF16 projections; the MXFP8
prefill tiles): their producer warps' TMA loads would have to follow the
wait as well. mxfp8_gemm_decode always chains; mxfp8_gemm never.

Scheduling only: no arithmetic, input or store order changes.
